.TH GRAFIC 1 "November 2026" "Grafic" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
grafic \- compose shaders, textures, and geometry
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B grafic gl
[\fB--stage\fR \fIfragment|vertex\fR]
[\fB--builtins\fR | \fB--preview-line\fR \fIN\fR]
.br
.B grafic tex
[\fB--width\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB--height\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB--seed\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB--preview-line\fR \fIN\fR]
.br
.B grafic mesh
[\fB--builtins\fR | \fB--preview-line\fR \fIN\fR]
.br
.B grafic lsp
.br
.B grafic view
[\fB--mesh\fR \fIFILE.gmesh\fR] [\fB--vert\fR \fIFILE.gvert\fR]
[\fB--frag\fR \fIFILE.gfrag\fR]
[\fB--width\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB--height\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB--preview-line\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB--tex0\fR \fIFILE.gtex\fR] ... [\fB--tex3\fR \fIFILE.gtex\fR]
[\fB--texture-width\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB--texture-height\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB--seed\fR \fIN\fR] \fIFILE.gfrag|FILE.gvert|FILE.gtex|FILE.gmesh\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Grafic composes graphics from chained transformations. Compiler commands read
source from standard input, write output to standard output, and report
diagnostics on standard error.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B gl
Compile .gfrag source to a GLSL 330 core fragment shader by default. Complete programs return
vec4. A rendering host supplies graficUv and displaced local-space graficPosition
inputs, u_time and u_resolution
uniforms, and any used texture inputs tex0 through tex3.
With --stage vertex, compile .gvert source returning a local-space vec3 position.
Inputs are position, uv, and time. Displaced position passes to fragments as
position, interpolated across triangles. Use position.y() for height colors
and first.mix(second, amount) to interpolate RGB colors. The host binds XYZ at attribute 0, UV at
attribute 1, and supplies u_model, u_view, u_projection, and u_time uniforms.
.TP
.B tex
Evaluate .gtex source to an RGBA PNG image. Complete programs return vec4.
The default width and height are 256 pixels; the default noise seed is zero.
.TP
.B mesh
Evaluate .gmesh source to a Wavefront OBJ mesh. Complete programs return mesh. Use grid().size(width, depth).subdivisions(x, z)
for an XZ grid with Y up, or disk() for an XY disk. Grid defaults are 2 by 2
units and 64 subdivisions per axis; counts range from 1 through 4096.
.TP
.B lsp
Run the shared language server over JSON-RPC on standard input and output.
It provides diagnostics, receiver-aware completion, and hover for mixed
shader, texture, and geometry documents. A recognized language ID (graficgl, graficvert,
grafictex, or graficmesh) selects the capability; otherwise the filename extension
is used. Unknown types receive a diagnostic and no completion or hover results.
.TP
.B view
Preview Grafic shader (.gfrag/.gvert), texture (.gtex), and mesh (.gmesh) sources with live reload. Supplies
time, resolution, and UV coordinates using an OpenGL 3.3 core context. Space
pauses or resumes animation; Escape closes the window. Errors go to standard
error and leave the last working shader and textures running. Bind procedural
texture sources with --tex0 through --tex3; each input reloads independently.
The default initial window size is 960 by 640. Press 1 for the shader or 2 through
5 for supplied tex0 through tex3 inputs. Switching preserves playback state.
The last show() call in each file selects its viewer output; normal compilation
treats show() as an identity function. An explicit --preview-line overrides
markers in the directly opened file.
Mesh previews use a fitted angled orthographic camera. Vertex sources use a
default subdivided XZ grid. Use --mesh FILE.gmesh, --vert FILE.gvert, and
--frag FILE.gfrag to compose geometry and shaders. Each source reloads independently.
Press W to toggle wireframe or U to toggle UV colors. Mesh show() markers require a mesh value and preserve normal OBJ export.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --stage " fragment|vertex"
Select the shader stage for gl. The default is fragment.
.TP
.B --builtins
Available on gl, tex, and mesh. Print the command's function signatures,
globals, and documentation.
.TP
.BI --preview-line " N"
Compile the intermediate result on a one-based source line. Fragment and texture
previews accept numeric or vector values; vertex previews require vec3 positions; geometry previews require a mesh.
.TP
.BI --width " N"
Set the texture width in pixels (tex), or initial window width (view).
.TP
.BI --height " N"
Set the texture height in pixels (tex), or initial window height (view).
.TP
.BI --seed " N"
Set the unsigned noise seed (tex default: zero; view default: 42).
.TP
.BI --tex0 " FILE.gtex"
Bind a procedural texture source to tex0 (view). Also accepts --tex1, --tex2,
and --tex3. Paths are relative to the working directory.
.TP
.BI --texture-width " N"
Set generated texture width in pixels (view, default: 512).
.TP
.BI --texture-height " N"
Set generated texture height in pixels (view, default: 512).
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show available commands or help for a subcommand.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
grafic gl < shader.gfrag > shader.frag
grafic gl --stage vertex < waves.gvert > waves.vert
grafic view waves.gvert --mesh surface.gmesh
grafic tex --width 512 --height 512 --seed 42 < clouds.gtex > clouds.png
grafic mesh < disk.gmesh > disk.obj
grafic gl --preview-line 4 < shader.gfrag > preview.frag
grafic view shader.gfrag
grafic view clouds.gtex
grafic view disk.gmesh
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns zero on success and nonzero for invalid commands, options, source,
or output. The viewer returns nonzero for startup failures; recoverable source
errors keep the window running. A selective build only provides its included
capabilities.
